# Reflection - Unit 3: Display Lists and Use Material Design

## What I Learned
- How to apply data classes, functions, and collections effectively in Kotlin.
- How to create simulated scrollable lists and implement click listeners.
- The main principles of Material Design, including colors, shapes, typography, and accessibility.

## Challenges
- Understanding how lists are connected and displayed through Android UI components.
- Applying Material Design guidelines through Kotlin-only simulations was challenging.
- Organizing collections and filtering data efficiently required additional practice.

## My Choices
- I used data classes to organize and represent structured product information.
- I simulated list scrolling and click listener interactions using Kotlin console output.
- I demonstrated Material Design principles through simple text-based simulations.

## Outcome
Unit 3 improved my understanding of how Kotlin fundamentals can be connected with user interface concepts.  
Although I did not fully use Android Studio, I practiced the logic behind lists, click listeners, and design principles, preparing me for practical Android UI development.
